<BaseLayout title="Engineering, version & methodology" description="Architecture, deterministic experiment scope, release identity and verification limits for Isaac Daroch’s static Astro–Quarto portfolio."><section class="section"><div class="shell prose"><p class="eyebrow">HOW THIS IS BUILT</p><h1>A living interface.<br/><em>A testable core.</em></h1><p class="lead">An Astro portfolio, a Quarto scientific notebook and an encapsulated educational laboratory, published as one static artifact.</p><h2>Architecture</h2><p>The laboratory’s domain and use cases are independent of the browser. Browser and headless adapters use the same public interface. The build integrates Quarto before verifying the final artifact. Dependencies, contracts and documentation are versioned together.</p><h2>What the checks establish</h2><p>Automated tests cover deterministic behavior, snapshots, input limits, policy comparisons, artifact integrity and browser interactions. They do not certify scientific generalization or replace manual testing with assistive technologies and representative devices.</p><h2>Version identity</h2><p><a href="/release.json">Machine-readable release manifest</a> records the source commit, toolchain and content digest. <a href="/artifact-manifest.json">The artifact inventory</a> identifies published files. Hashes describe content integrity, not authorship of imported episodes.</p><h2>Source and governing documentation</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/Isaac-Daroch/Isaac-Daroch.github.io">Inspect the repository</a>, its D2 requirements, architecture decisions, change records and validation workflows. The first integrated source is reconstructed against D2; it is not represented as a byte-for-byte copy of the earlier uncommitted archive.</p><h2>Known verification limits</h2><p>Human screen-reader task studies, long-term field performance and measurements on the owner’s laboratory/personal computers remain separate evaluations. A green software workflow is not a certificate of complete WCAG conformance.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
